   </div></details></nav></div></header><script>(function(){var d=document.querySelector(".mnav");if(!d)return;document.addEventListener("click",function(e){if(d.open&&!d.contains(e.target))d.open=false});document.addEventListener("keydown",function(e){if(e.key==="Escape"&&d.open){d.open=false;d.querySelector("summary").focus()}})})();</script><main><nav class="crumb w" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <span>Board compliance</span></nav><section class="hero w hv"><div><h1>Board of Nursing Compliance for Nursing Programs</h1><p class="lead">Vexcura checks your program's clinical hours, simulation use, ratios, faculty and preceptor records, NCLEX standard and annual report against your state board's rules. Every requirement is cited, and you see what needs attention while there's still time to fix it. For Georgia, Tennessee and Alabama programs, in every plan.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/for-nursing-schools#pilot">Request a demo</a><a class="btn alt" href="#boards">For boards of nursing</a></div></div><figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/bc-dean-1000.webp" srcset="/img/bc-dean-1600.webp 1600w, /img/bc-dean-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 860px) calc(100vw - 32px), 580px" width="1000" height="625" alt="The school's board compliance workspace for a fictional Georgia ADN program: counts of Not met, At risk, Not enough data and Met, the report button, sharing status and alerts" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>The board compliance workspace for a fictional Georgia ADN program. Demo data.</figcaption></figure></section><div class="w"><p class="soon"><b>Rules verified November 6, 2026</b> · confirm with your board; not legal advice.</p>
       <h2>What it covers</h2><div class="tw"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Board and rules</th><th>ADN</th><th>BSN</th><th>PN</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>Georgia</b></td><td>Georgia Board of Nursing<br><small>Ga. Comp. R. &amp; Regs. ch. 410-8 (RN) and 410-9 (PN)</small></td><td>16</td><td>16</td><td>17</td></tr><tr><td><b>Tennessee</b></td><td>Tennessee Board of Nursing<br><small>Tenn. Comp. R. &amp; Regs. ch. 1000-01 (.09 to .15)</small></td><td>16</td><td>16</td><td>16</td></tr><tr><td><b>Alabama</b></td><td>Alabama Board of Nursing<br><small>Ala. Admin. Code ch. 610-X-3</small></td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>15</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
       <p>That's 142 cited requirements across clinical hours and clinical areas, simulation limits, faculty and preceptor ratios and qualifications, curriculum, the board's NCLEX first-time pass-rate standard, the annual report, records, student requirements and clinical sites. Where a state sets no rule, the workspace says "No state rule" instead of inventing one. Proposed rules, such as Georgia's proposed 50% simulation limit, are shown but not counted, and a board position statement, such as Tennessee's simulation limit, is labeled as one.</p>
       <h2>Four statuses, one per requirement</h2><div class="feat"><div><b>Met</b>Your records meet the requirement.</div><div><b>At risk</b>Not failing yet, but trending that way, or the rule's meaning needs confirming with your board.</div><div><b>Not met</b>Your records show the requirement isn't met.</div><div><b>Not enough data</b>Something the check needs hasn't been recorded yet.</div></div>
       <div class="split"><div class="st"><h2>Every requirement is cited</h2><p>Open any requirement to see what the rule says, the citation with a link, its effective date where the source shows one, the date Vexcura verified it, whether it's a rule or a position statement, and the clinical days or records behind the status.</p><p>NCLEX results appear only as the numbers your program enters, measured against your board's standard.</p></div><figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/bc-drill-1000.webp" srcset="/img/bc-drill-1600.webp 1600w, /img/bc-drill-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="A requirement drill-down: Met, the rule text, its citation, effective and verified dates, and the clinical days behind the status. Fictional program and site" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>A requirement drill-down. Fictional program and site.</figcaption></figure></div>
       <h2>Built on the records you already keep</h2><ul><li><b>Clinical hours come from clinical days.</b> Only signed-in attendance (present or late) counts, and past days nobody marked show up as an alert.</li><li><b>Alerts while there's time.</b> For example, a student who can't reach a course's planned hours even with every scheduled day, with buttons to schedule clinical or assign simulation hours.</li><li><b>Faculty and preceptor credentials</b> are what your program records after checking them. Vexcura never stores license numbers.</li><li><b>Rule changes to watch,</b> such as pending amendments, appear as notices on your program.</li></ul>
       <div class="split rev"><div class="st"><h2>The self-report PDF</h2><p>Download a program-generated self-report: summary counts, then each requirement with the rule, what was found, the citation and the verified date, plus any notices about pending rule changes. Every page says it's program-generated and not an official board document.</p><p>Student names are optional. An "Include student names" box controls the student hour list and named alerts.</p></div><figure class="shot"><img src="/img/bc-report-800.webp" srcset="/img/bc-report-1200.webp 1200w, /img/bc-report-800.webp 800w" sizes="(max-width: 860px) calc(100vw - 32px), 480px" width="800" height="642" alt="Page 1 of a program-generated board compliance self-report PDF for a fictional program, marked not an official board document" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>Page 1 of a self-report for a fictional program.</figcaption></figure></div>
       <h2>Sharing is the school's choice</h2><p>Your program decides whether its board sees anything. Only the school's program admin can turn sharing on or off; Vexcura can't. Turning it on records an acknowledgment that the program is sharing its compliance summary, clinical-hour totals and simulation use with the board, as aggregate counts only, with no student names or IDs. Every change is written to the audit log, and sharing can be turned off at any time.</p>
       <h2 id="boards">For boards of nursing: a free, read-only portal</h2><p>Board staff see the programs in their state that chose to share. For each one: its overall status; the counts of Not met, At risk, Not enough data and Met; students, clinical days, direct-care and simulation hours, the simulation share, and faculty and preceptors recorded; hours by clinical area; and each requirement with its citation. Counts of 1 to 4 in lines and alerts show as "fewer than 5."</p>
       <p>Each summary is program-generated from the program's own records, not a board determination. Board accounts are free and set up by Vexcura on request, with no public sign-up. Board staff can call <a href="tel:+17626772802">762-677-2802</a>.</p>
       <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/bc-program-1000.webp" srcset="/img/bc-program-1600.webp 1600w, /img/bc-program-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="The read-only board portal for a demo board account: a fictional ADN program's program-generated summary with students, clinical days, direct care and simulation hours, and each cited requirement marked Met, Not met or Not enough data" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>A program summary in the board portal, for a demo board account and a fictional program.</figcaption></figure>
       <h2>What it isn't</h2><ul><li>It isn't legal advice or a determination of compliance. Confirm with your board.</li><li>It doesn't file anything with your board. You file your annual report the way you do now and mark it submitted.</li><li>It doesn't store students' background checks or immunization records, or handle clinical placement. Where a board requires student policies, the program confirms them.</li></ul>
       <p class="src" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px">Vexcura is independent and isn't affiliated with or endorsed by the Georgia Board of Nursing, the Tennessee Board of Nursing, the Alabama Board of Nursing or NCSBN. Board names are used only to identify the rules each profile covers. Screens show fictional programs, students and sites and a demo board account.</p>
       <h2 id="pricing">Included in every plan</h2><p>Board compliance is included in every Vexcura plan, and boards use the portal free. Plans differ only in how many students they cover, per year: Per student $199 per student seat · Site 100 $15,000 · Site 250 $30,000 · Site 500 $50,000 · Custom: Custom quote. <a href="/for-nursing-schools#pricing">Pricing for schools</a></p>
       <h2>Common questions</h2><details class="faq"><summary>Which states and programs does it cover?</summary><p>Georgia, Tennessee and Alabama, for ADN, BSN and practical nursing (PN) programs: 142 cited requirements in all. Rules were verified on November 6, 2026.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>What does it check?</summary><p>Clinical hours and clinical areas, simulation limits, faculty-to-student and preceptor ratios, faculty and preceptor qualifications, curriculum, the board's NCLEX first-time pass-rate standard, the annual report, records, student requirements and clinical sites, as each state's rules set them.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Is this legal advice or a board determination?</summary><p>No. It's a program-generated summary of your own records against each rule as Vexcura reads it. Confirm with your board; it isn't legal advice, and it isn't a determination of compliance.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Who can share our summary with the board?</summary><p>Only your school's program admin can turn sharing on or off, and Vexcura can't. Sharing sends aggregate counts only, with no student names or IDs, and every change is written to the audit log. You can turn it off at any time.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Do boards of nursing pay?</summary><p>No. Board portal accounts are free and read-only. Vexcura sets them up for board staff on request; there's no public sign-up.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does the PDF include student names?</summary><p>Only if you choose. An &quot;Include student names&quot; box controls the student hour list and named alerts. Every page says the report is program-generated and isn't an official board document.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does Vexcura file our annual report?</summary><p>No. You file with your board the way you do now. The workspace tracks the due date, and you mark the report submitted once it's filed.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>What does it cost?</summary><p>Board compliance is included in every plan, and boards never pay. The school or facility licenses Vexcura: Per student $199 per student seat; Site 100 $15,000; Site 250 $30,000; Site 500 $50,000; Custom Custom quote, per year.</p></details><h2>More for nursing programs</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/for-nursing-schools">Vexcura for nursing schools</a></li><li><a href="/clinical-instructor-tools">Clinical instructor tools</a></li><li><a href="/academic-ehr-for-nursing-students">Academic EHR for nursing students</a></li><li><a href="/nursing-simulation-scenarios">Nursing simulation scenarios and drills</a></li><li><a href="/virtual-nursing-simulation">Virtual nursing simulation (VR coming soon)</a></li><li><a href="/nursing-lms-integration">Canvas, Blackboard, D2L and Moodle integration</a></li></ul></div><section class="band vxs-band"><div class="vxs-bg" data-vxs-i="0" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="vxs-sh" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="w"><h2>Try Vexcura with one cohort for a semester, free</h2><p>Pick one clinical group or course. Faculty accounts are always free. At the end of the semester you decide whether to license it for your program; there's no obligation to buy, and every plan includes everything. Founding programs: 50% off the first paid year.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/for-nursing-schools#pilot">Request a pilot</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools">How licensing works</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="foot"><div class="w"><div class="cols">
